.TH DAGNABIT 1 "2026-06-19" "dagnabit 0.1.0" "Developer Tools"
.SH NAME
dagnabit \- reposition Go packages and Rust crates by dependency depth and generate export facades
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dagnabit
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-depth
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-initial ]
.RB [ \-lang
.IR go | rust ]
.RB [ \-module
.IR path ]
.IR prefix ...
.PP
.B dagnabit export
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-output\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-library ]
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.RB [ \-\-copy ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-rewrite\-consumers ]
.RB [ \-lang
.IR go | rust ]
.RB [ \-module
.IR path ]
.RI [ packages... ]
.PP
.B dagnabit move
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-lang
.IR go | rust ]
.RB [ \-module
.IR path ]
.IR src
.IR dst
.PP
.B dagnabit rename
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-lang
.IR go | rust ]
.RB [ \-module
.IR path ]
.IR src
.RI [ new\-leaf ]
.PP
.B dagnabit init-smoke
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-module
.IR path ]
.PP
.B dagnabit version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dagnabit
is a code organization tool for Go modules and cargo (Rust) workspaces
with five subcommands: repositioning, export facade generation, package
relocation
.RB ( move ),
single-package repositioning
.RB ( rename ),
and per-arch init-smoke test generation
.RB ( init-smoke ,
go-only).
The operating language is auto-detected; see
.BR LANGUAGES .
.PP
Without a subcommand,
.B dagnabit
analyzes the dependency graph of packages, computes a topological sort,
and moves packages into directories named after NATO phonetic levels
based on their dependency depth.
Leaf packages (no internal dependencies) go to level 0, their
dependents to alfa, and so on up through the NATO alphabet.
In go mode the graph comes from
.BR "go list" ;
in rust mode from
.BR "cargo metadata" .
.PP
The
.B export
subcommand generates facade packages that re-export symbols from
.I internal/
packages, creating a public API surface in
.IR pkgs/ .
In go mode, types are re-exported as aliases, non-generic functions and
variables as var bindings, and constants as const bindings.
Generic functions are wrapped because Go does not support assigning
them to variables without instantiation (see
.UR https://github.com/golang/go/issues/52654
golang/go#52654\c
.UE ).
Functions whose signatures reference unexported types are skipped.
Go code generation uses
.B jennifer
(github.com/dave/jennifer) for proper import management.
In rust mode, facades are one-line glob re-export crates; see the
.B export
subsection under
.BR SUBCOMMANDS .
.SH LANGUAGES
.B dagnabit
operates on Go modules (go mode) and cargo workspaces (rust mode).
The mode is auto-detected by walking up from the current directory; the
first directory containing either marker wins:
.TP
.B go.mod
go mode.
.TP
.B Cargo.toml containing a [workspace] table
rust mode. A crate-only
.B Cargo.toml
(a
.B [package]
table without
.BR [workspace] )
does not count; the walk continues upward past it.
.PP
Finding both markers in the same directory, or neither anywhere up to
the filesystem root, is an error. Pass
.B \-lang go
or
.B \-lang rust
to disambiguate;
.B \-lang
also restricts the upward walk to the named language's marker.
.PP
Both modes operate on the detected root: the directory containing
.I go.mod
(go) or the workspace
.I Cargo.toml
(rust). Either mode may be invoked from any subdirectory beneath its
root. Prefix arguments and package paths are always interpreted
relative to that root, not the invocation directory.
.PP
The
.B \-module
flag is go-only; combining it with rust mode is an error.
.SS "Runtime requirements (rust mode)"
Rust mode shells out to
.BR cargo (1),
which must be on
.BR PATH .
Crate renames
.RB ( move
or
.B rename
with a differing leaf) additionally require
.B ast-grep
for dependent-source rewrites. The Nix package wraps the
.B dagnabit
binary with ast-grep appended to
.B PATH
as a fallback; a user-provided ast-grep earlier on
.B PATH
wins.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS "reposition (default)"
Analyze and reposition packages based on dependency depth.
In go mode, must be run from a directory containing
.IR go.mod .
.PP
In rust mode, crates are the unit of repositioning. The dependency
graph is read from
.BR "cargo metadata \-\-format\-version 1 \-\-no\-deps" ;
only path-dependencies that resolve to workspace members contribute
edges (registry dependencies are ignored). Moving a crate rewrites the
relative path-dependencies the move invalidated in every member
.B Cargo.toml
plus the
.B [workspace]
members entry in the root manifest; no
.I .rs
file is touched (crate names do not change in a pure move). Each move
is gated by re-running
.B cargo metadata
to verify the workspace still resolves.
.SS "move"
Relocate a single package from
.I src
to
.I dst
(both relative to the module or workspace root).
.PP
In go mode, when the leaf directory name differs between
.I src
and
.IR dst ,
.B move
performs type-aware rewrites of the package's
.B package
declaration and of qualified references (e.g.,
.IB oldLeaf .X
\(->
.IB newLeaf .X )
in every caller, using
.B golang.org/x/tools/go/packages
to discriminate package uses from local variables, aliased imports, and
dot-imports.
A pre-move analysis aborts if
.B packages.Load
reports any type errors in the module. Pass
.B \-\-force
to proceed anyway.
.PP
In rust mode, a move whose leaf is unchanged is a pure directory move
with Cargo.toml-only rewrites, exactly as in
.BR reposition .
When the leaf differs, the move is a crate rename: in addition to the
directory move and manifest path-dependency rewrites,
.B dagnabit
rewrites the crate's
.B [package]
name (preserving the
.IB <name> _internal
convention:
.IB oldLeaf _internal
\(->
.IB newLeaf _internal ),
renames the dependency key in every directly dependent member's
.BR Cargo.toml ,
and rewrites source references in those dependents via
.B ast-grep
using a single whole-identifier pattern (the old lib-target identifier
\(-> the new one), which matches use declarations, qualified
expressions, and type positions without substring false positives.
.PP
Rust renames are gated by
.B cargo check \-\-workspace
both before and after the rewrite;
.B \-\-force
skips only the pre-flight check. Independent of
.BR \-\-force ,
a rename always verifies ast-grep is on
.B PATH
and fails fast if a generated facade
.IB pkgs/ oldLeaf
exists, before any tree mutation: facades are generated, not renamed;
remove it and re-run
.B dagnabit export
after the rename. On a post-flight failure the tree is left dirty for
inspection.
.SS "rename"
Reposition ONE package (go) or crate (rust) to the NATO level dictated
by its transitive internal dependencies, optionally renaming its leaf.
Other packages are NOT moved, even if they sit at the wrong level; use
the default reposition subcommand to rebalance the whole tree.
.PP
The destination is computed, not given: the leaf is kept (or replaced
by
.IR new\-leaf ,
when given) and the level segment is replaced by the computed one. The
actual move delegates to
.BR move ,
so the per-language rewrite and gating behavior described there applies
unchanged. In go mode,
.I src
is a two-component
.I <level>/<leaf>
path; in rust mode it must be a three-component
.I <prefix>/<level>/<leaf>
path.
.SS "export"
Generate facades from
.I internal/
packages into the output directory (default
.IR pkgs/ ).
.PP
Three invocation modes:
.TP
.B "dagnabit export"
Scan
.I internal/
for opted-in packages and generate facades for each. In go mode, a
package opts in with a
.B //go:generate dagnabit export
directive in a source file; in rust mode, with
.B [package.metadata.dagnabit] export = true
in the crate manifest.
.TP
.BI "dagnabit export " packages...
Generate facades for the specified packages (go: package patterns such
as
.BR ./internal/alfa/... ;
rust: crate directories relative to the workspace root, such as
.BR internal/alfa/store ).
.TP
.B "dagnabit export \-\-library"
Export every package under
.IR internal/ .
In go mode this fails if any
.B //go:generate dagnabit export
directives exist; in rust mode it exports every crate under
.IR internal/ .
.PP
In go mode, after generation,
.B dagnabit
runs the project formatter on the output directory when a
.BR conformist (1)
configuration
.RB ( conformist.toml
or
.BR .conformist.toml )
is present. The config is found by walking up from the module root,
bounded by
.B DAGNABIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES
(see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ):
the walk never ascends into a ceiling directory, so a repo whose own config is
.B Nix\-generated
(no
.B conformist.toml
on disk) does not escalate to a stray ancestor config. For such a repo, set
.B DAGNABIT_CONFORMIST_CONFIG
to the generated config path; this short\-circuits the search and runs
.B conformist \-\-config\-file
with that config. When a config is found but
.B conformist
is not on
.BR PATH ,
.B dagnabit
fails rather than silently emitting unformatted facades. This is skipped
under
.B \-\-dry\-run
and when no config is found.
.PP
In rust mode, facades are glob re-export crates: for an internal crate
at
.IB internal/<level>/ name
whose
.B [package]
name is
.IB name _internal\fR,\fP
.B export
generates
.IB pkgs/ name /Cargo.toml
(a single path-dependency on the internal crate) and
.IB pkgs/ name /src/lib.rs
containing
.BI "pub use " name "_internal::*;"
and idempotently adds the facade to the root
.B [workspace]
members. Internal crates MUST follow the
.IB <name> _internal
package-name convention; an internal crate whose
.B [package]
name equals its facade name is an error.
.B No
formatter pass runs on rust facades: the generated output is
byte-canonical (rustfmt-clean) by construction, keeping
.B export
and
.B \-\-check
environment-independent.
.SS "init-smoke"
Generate per-arch blank-import tests that catch package
.B init()
functions which fail on a particular
.IR GOOS / GOARCH .
Such an init compiles clean on every arch and detonates only at module
.I instantiation
on the arch that cannot satisfy it (e.g. a
.I /dev/null
open under the js/wasm strict filesystem), so it is invisible to
.B go build
and caught only by running the module. Go-only.
.PP
Target arches are declared in
.I dagnabit.toml
at the module root, as
.B [[init-smoke.arch]]
entries with
.BR goos ", " goarch ", " loader ", and " skip
keys. For each arch,
.B dagnabit
type-checks the module's package graph under that
.IR GOOS / GOARCH
(via
.BR golang.org/x/tools/go/packages )
and writes
.IB initsmoke/ initsmoke_ goos _ goarch _test.go\fR,\fP
a
.BR //go:build \-constrained
file that blank-imports every package which
.I builds
for the arch. Packages that do not build for the arch are auto-excluded;
.B skip
lists packages that build but should be excluded anyway (a
.B skip
entry matching no package is an error). Instantiating the generated test
binary runs every imported package's
.BR init() ,
so a per-arch init hazard surfaces as a load-time panic naming the offender.
.PP
Like
.BR export ,
.B init-smoke
runs the project formatter on the generated files (honoring
.B DAGNABIT_CONFORMIST_CONFIG
/
.BR DAGNABIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES ;
see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ),
and
.B \-\-check
regenerates into a temporary directory and byte-compares against the
committed files, exiting nonzero and naming the out-of-sync arch files on
drift.
.SS "version"
Print the build identity \(em version and commit \(em of the
.B dagnabit
binary, then exit. Output is a single self\-identification line per
.BR eng\-versioning (7):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit VERSION+COMMIT
.fi
.RE
.PP
The values are injected at link time by the Nix build (from the
repo\-root
.IR version.env ).
A plain
.B "go build"
without those ldflags reports
.BR dev+unknown .
The same identity is stamped into the
.B "Code generated by dagnabit (VERSION+COMMIT)"
header of every exported facade, so a stale binary run against a newer
library surfaces as facade drift rather than a silent compile error.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IR prefix ...
One or more package tree prefixes to analyze (e.g.
.BR lib ", " internal ", " src ).
At least one prefix is required for the reposition subcommand.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Reposition options"
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be moved without moving.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BI \-depth " N"
Path component depth: 3 for
.I prefix/level/package
(default), 2 for
.IR level/package .
Use depth 2 for repos where NATO levels are top-level directories.
Implied (and overridden) by
.BR \-\-initial .
.TP
.B \-\-initial
Initial tiering of a flat
.I <prefix>/<pkg>
layout. Inserts a NATO level segment into every package path based on
its dependency height, producing
.IR <prefix>/<level>/<pkg> .
Implies
.BR "\-depth 2" .
.TP
.BI \-lang " go|rust"
Operating language. Auto-detected when empty (see
.BR LANGUAGES ).
.TP
.BI \-module " path"
Go module path. Read from
.I go.mod
if empty. Go-only.
.SS "Move options"
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be moved without moving: a
.B would-move
event is emitted for the planned move. In rust mode, a leaf rename
additionally prints the rename plan with per-pattern ast-grep match
counts (same-leaf moves print only the planned move).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Go: proceed even if
.B packages.Load
reports type errors. Rewrites may miss call sites in packages with type
errors; use only when the errors are unrelated to the moved package.
Rust: skip the
.B cargo check \-\-workspace
pre-flight gate (the post-flight gate still runs).
.TP
.BI \-lang " go|rust"
Operating language. Auto-detected when empty (see
.BR LANGUAGES ).
.TP
.BI \-module " path"
Go module path. Read from
.I go.mod
if empty. Go-only.
.SS "Rename options"
Same flags as
.BR move :
.BR \-n / \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-v / \-\-verbose ,
.BR \-\-force ,
.BI \-lang " go|rust"
and the go-only
.BI \-module " path"
all behave identically.
.SS "Export options"
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be generated without writing files.
.TP
.BI \-output\-dir " dir"
Output directory for generated facades, relative to the module or
workspace root (default:
.BR pkgs ).
.TP
.B \-\-library
Export facades for every package under
.IR internal/ .
Does not accept package arguments. Go mode fails if any
.B //go:generate dagnabit export
directives exist.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
Verify the committed facades match a fresh export without writing:
regenerate into a temporary directory, byte-compare against the
committed tree, and exit nonzero on drift. Works with
.BR \-\-library ,
explicit packages, or the directive scan.
.TP
.B \-\-copy
Copy internal source files into
.IR pkgs/ ,
rewriting only intra-module imports, instead of emitting thin re-export
aliases. Go-only.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rewrite\-consumers
Skip rewriting external workspace consumers' imports to the new facade
path. Go-only.
.TP
.BI \-lang " go|rust"
Operating language. Auto-detected when empty (see
.BR LANGUAGES ).
.TP
.BI \-module " path"
Go module path. Read from
.I go.mod
if empty. Go-only.
.SS "Init-smoke options"
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
Verify the committed init-smoke tests match a fresh generation without
writing: regenerate into a temporary directory, byte-compare against the
committed
.I initsmoke/
files, and exit nonzero (naming the out-of-sync arch files) on drift.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Enumerate and render without writing files.
.TP
.BI \-module " path"
Go module path. Read from
.I go.mod
if empty.
.SH EXAMPLES
Reposition packages in a repo with
.I lib/
and
.I internal/
prefixes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cd myproject
dagnabit -n -v lib internal
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reposition packages in a repo where NATO levels are top-level:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit -n -v -depth 2 0 alfa bravo charlie
.fi
.RE
.PP
Initial tiering of a flat
.I internal/<pkg>
layout (produces
.IR internal/0/<pkg> ", " internal/alfa/<pkg> ", \fR\(aq.\(aq\fP\ etc.):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit -n -v --initial internal
.fi
.RE
.PP
Relocate a package with a leaf rename (rewrites package decl, imports,
and qualified references in callers):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit move internal/foo internal/bar
.fi
.RE
.PP
Relocate without renaming the leaf (same leaf, imports-only rewrite):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit move internal/alfa/foo internal/bravo/foo
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dry-run a move to preview what would change:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit move -n internal/foo internal/bar
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate export facades for all marked internal packages:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit export
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate facades for specific packages:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit export ./internal/alfa/blob_store_id ./internal/bravo/...
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dry-run to see what would be generated:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit export -n ./internal/...
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dry-run a repositioning of cargo workspace crates under
.I internal/
(runs from any subdirectory of the workspace):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit -n -v -lang rust internal
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate glob facades for every internal crate of a cargo workspace:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit export --library
.fi
.RE
.PP
Move a crate with a rename (rewrites the [package] name, dependents'
dependency keys, and dependents' sources via ast-grep, gated by
.BR "cargo check" ):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit move internal/alfa/store internal/alfa/blob_store
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify the committed rust facades are in sync without writing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit export --check --library
.fi
.RE
.PP
Regenerate the per-arch init-smoke tests, then verify they are in sync:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit init-smoke
dagnabit init-smoke --check   # exit 1 + arch file list on drift
.fi
.RE
.SH GENERATED OUTPUT
In go mode, for an internal package at
.IR internal/alfa/blob_store_id ,
dagnabit generates
.IR pkgs/blob_store_id/main.go :
.PP
.RS
.nf
// Code generated by dagnabit (dev+unknown); DO NOT EDIT.

package blob_store_id

import internal "example.com/mod/internal/alfa/blob_store_id"

type (
    Id           = internal.Id
    LocationType = internal.LocationType
)

var (
    Make             = internal.Make
    MakeWithLocation = internal.MakeWithLocation
)
.fi
.RE
.PP
In rust mode, for an internal crate at
.I internal/alfa/blob_store_id
whose
.B [package]
name is
.BR blob_store_id_internal ,
dagnabit generates
.I pkgs/blob_store_id/Cargo.toml
and
.IR pkgs/blob_store_id/src/lib.rs :
.PP
.RS
.nf
[package]
name = "blob_store_id"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"

[dependencies]
blob_store_id_internal = { path = "../../internal/alfa/blob_store_id" }
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS
.nf
// Code generated by dagnabit (dev+unknown); DO NOT EDIT.

pub use blob_store_id_internal::*;
.fi
.RE
.SH DIRECTIVES
In go mode, place the following comment in any
.I .go
file within an internal package to mark it for export:
.PP
.RS
.B //go:generate dagnabit export
.RE
.PP
In rust mode, the analog is a manifest key in the internal crate's
.BR Cargo.toml :
.PP
.RS
.nf
[package.metadata.dagnabit]
export = true
.fi
.RE
.PP
When
.B dagnabit export
is run without arguments, it scans
.I internal/
for these markers.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DAGNABIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES
Colon\-separated list of absolute directories above which
.B dagnabit
will not walk when searching upward from the module root for a formatter
configuration. Mirrors
.BR GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES :
a ceiling entry is the last directory not searched, so directories at and below
the ceiling (including the module root) are still checked. Use it to stop a repo
with a Nix\-generated conformist config from escalating to a stray ancestor
.B conformist.toml
(such as an eng\-root config).
.TP
.B DAGNABIT_CONFORMIST_CONFIG
Absolute path to an explicit
.B conformist
config file. When set, the upward configuration search is skipped entirely and
.B dagnabit
runs
.B conformist \-\-config\-file
with this path. Intended for repositories whose conformist config is
Nix\-generated and therefore not present on disk as a
.B conformist.toml
(see
.BR DESCRIPTION ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (dependency cycle, missing
.I go.mod
or
.B [workspace]
.IR Cargo.toml ,
generation failure, failed cargo gate, etc.).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go-generate (1),
.BR go-list (1),
.BR conformist (1),
.BR cargo (1),
.BR cargo-metadata (1),
.BR cargo-check (1),
.BR ast-grep (1)
